@startuml
title Core sharding: two independent CI jobs
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
hide footbox

participant "CI pipeline" as ci #F1F5F9
participant "Job 1\nisolated workspace" as one
participant "Job 2\nisolated workspace" as two
participant "CI reports / status" as reports #F1F5F9

note over ci,reports
  Same consumer + plugin revisions, task, selection, history and count = 2.
  Only index differs. No shared writable build directory.
end note

ci -> one : Start Test task; index = 1
ci -> two : Start Test task; index = 2

par Job 1
  one -> one : Build local ownership plan
  one -> one : Exclude families not owned by 1
  one -> one : Gradle / framework execute retained tests
  one -> reports : Job 1 status + separate reports
else Job 2
  two -> two : Build same local ownership plan
  two -> two : Exclude families not owned by 2
  two -> two : Gradle / framework execute retained tests
  two -> reports : Job 2 status + separate reports
end

reports -> ci : Gate pipeline on all required job results

note over one,two
  No communication between shards.
  Empty shards can be legitimate; normal test failures still fail.
end note

note over ci,reports
  Scheduling, artifact collection and global completion checks belong to CI.
  Optional manifest verification checks collected class selections.
  It does not merge test reports or prove successful job completion.
end note
@enduml
